# This repo does NOT read this file. It documents the runtime secrets the app
# needs, which are deployed from GitHub on every deploy.
#
#   GitHub secret:  DEPLOY_TEST=abc   (environment: staging / prod)
#   server file:    /opt/apps/<slug>/.env.<stage>  ->  TEST=abc
#
# To add a secret:
#   1. Add it as an environment secret named DEPLOY_<NAME> in both the staging
#      and prod environments (same name, different values).
#   2. In .github/workflows/deploy.yml, map it in the deploy jobs' env:
#         DEPLOY_<NAME>: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_<NAME> }}
#
# `scripts/deploy.sh` strips the DEPLOY_ prefix and writes <NAME>=value into the
# server's .env.<stage>. The compose overrides load it via `env_file`.
#
# Demo secret: DEPLOY_TEST -> app sees TEST
# Real app examples:
#   DEPLOY_GRAPHDB_URL=https://graphdb.katharsis.digital
#   DEPLOY_GRAPHDB_USER=svc-myapp
#   DEPLOY_GRAPHDB_PASSWORD=change-me
